ype checkers fail.","file":"api/services/billing_service.py","line":292,"severity":"high","side":"RIGHT","title":"Skip invalid plans instead of returning None"},{"description":"The Python Style CI runs mypy, which rejects this __str__ definition with 'Invalid statement in TypedDict definition; expected field_name: field_type'. TypedDict values are ordinary dicts, so the method does not supply the advertised string representation either. Remove it from SubscriptionPlan and use a separate formatting helper if needed.","endLine":30,"failureMode":"Python Style CI fails on an invalid method in the TypedDict schema.","file":"api/services/billing_service.py","line":28,"severity":"high","side":"RIGHT","title":"Remove the method from the TypedDict schema"},{"description":"When REDIS_USE_CLUSTERS is enabled, keys such as tenant_plan:tenant-1 and tenant_plan:tenant-2 occupy different slots. RedisCluster.mget rejects this batch, so even an all-hit request always calls the billing API; if the API is unavailable, it returns no plans despite a healthy populated cache. Read via a cluster-safe pipeline of GETs or equivalent per-slot batching.","endLine":323,"failureMode":"Bulk requests on a supported Redis Cluster deployment cannot read their cached plans and repeatedly call the billing API.","file":"api/services/billing_service.py","line":323,"severity":"medium","side":"RIGHT","title":"Use a cluster-safe bulk cache read"},{"description":"The new cache-validation path uses the existing unconfigured TypedDict adapter, which ignores extra fields. A Redis record containing plan, expiration_date, and an undeclared field is therefore accepted as a hit instead of rejected and refetched. AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md Rule 14 requires Pydantic v2 validation that forbids extras by default; configure the cache record schema accordingly.","endLine":340,"failureMode":"A cached record with undeclared fields bypasses the mandated extra-field validation and suppresses the billing API refresh.","file":"api/services/billing_service.py","line":339,"severity":"medium","side":"RIGHT","title":"Reject undeclared fields in cached plan records"},{"description":"When Redis mget fails in a batch job, the new exception log contains no tenant identifiers. The global log filter supplies request/trace IDs, not tenant context, and batch jobs need not have a request. Operators cannot determine which tenant batch fell back to the API; include tenant_ids as required by Rule 23.","endLine":355,"failureMode":"Redis-read failure output lacks the affected tenant batch, preventing required tenant-level diagnosis.","file":"api/services/billing_service.py","line":355,"severity":"low","side":"RIGHT","title":"Identify tenants in the cache-read failure log"},{"description":"When the Redis pipeline fails, this new error log omits all tenant identifiers, so operators cannot identify the batch whose plans were not cached. Rule 23 requires object identifiers in the log context, and the global formatter does not add tenant IDs. Include the affected bulk_plans keys in this event.","endLine":385,"failureMode":"Pipeline-failure output cannot identify the tenants whose cache writes failed.","file":"api/services/billing_service.py","line":385,"severity":"low","side":"RIGHT","title":"Identify tenants in the cache-write failure log"},{"description":"In batch jobs this new event emits only hit/miss counts, so operators cannot correlate cache-read statistics with the tenants covered. Rule 23 requires tenant/app/workflow identifiers in log context, and the global formatter adds only trace/request IDs. Include tenant_ids in this event.","endLine":352,"failureMode":"Cache-read statistics cannot be correlated with the affected tenant batch, violating the mandatory logging-context contract.","file":"api/services/billing_service.py","line":350,"severity":"low","side":"RIGHT","title":"Identify tenants in cache-read statistics"},{"description":"This cache-write event records only the number of plans, so concurrent tenant batches produce output that cannot identify which tenants were cached. Rule 23 requires tenant/app/workflow identifiers; neither the formatter nor OTEL supplies them. Include the bulk_plans tenant IDs in this event.","endLine":382,"failureMode":"Successful cache-write events cannot be correlated with their tenant batches.","file":"api/services/billing_service.py","line":381,"severity":"low","side":"RIGHT","title":"Identify tenants in the cache-write log"}],"lens":"focal-discovery","model":"openai/gpt-6.1-sol","reviewerId":"focal-discovery","severity":"high"},"wallMs":1520246.9427919998,"passes":{"finder":{"modelReported":"gpt-6.1-sol","promptHash":"a8c41f9e0562bd8ddcb58aa20a67584894de1e1eb004519031d9d9c896ce11e8","turns":18,"usage":{"cacheCreation":0,"cached":1881600,"input":186803,"output":34574,"reasoning":20324,"total":2102977},"wallMs":1516070.537958}}}}]}